# WN22-00-000380: Windows Server 2022 must not the Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol installed.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-00-000380-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must not the Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol installed.`
    description `SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks and is not FIPS compliant.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,windows-feature,medium,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:CM-7`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Uninstall the SMBv1 protocol. Open "Windows PowerShell" with elevated privileges (run as administrator). Enter "Uninstall-WindowsFeature -Name FS-SMB1 -Restart". (Omit the Restart parameter if an immediate restart of the system cannot be done.) Alternately: Start "Server Manager". Select the server with the feature. Scroll down to "ROLES AND FEATURES" in the right pane. Select "Remove Roles and Features" from the drop-down "TASKS" list. Select the appropriate server on the "Server Selection" pag`

    component_id `comp-windows-feature`

    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by keeping the 'FS-SMB1' Windows Server feature/role uninstalled. The ESP scanner queries the feature via the windows_feature CTN (Get-WindowsFeature) and fails the policy if the feature is Installed. Remediation uninstalls the feature via Uninstall-WindowsFeature or Server Manager.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by keeping the 'FS-SMB1' Windows Server feature/role uninstalled. The ESP scanner queries the feature via the windows_feature CTN (Get-WindowsFeature) and fails the policy if the feature is Installed. Remediation uninstalls the feature via Uninstall-WindowsFeature or Server Manager.`
    impl_CM_7 `Windows Server implements CM-7 by keeping the 'FS-SMB1' Windows Server feature/role uninstalled. The ESP scanner queries the feature via the windows_feature CTN (Get-WindowsFeature) and fails the policy if the feature is Installed. Remediation uninstalls the feature via Uninstall-WindowsFeature or Server Manager.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        name `FS-SMB1`
        behavior executor windowsfeature
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        enabled boolean = false
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_feature
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
